Metric:
- id: usage.creators_ratio
- name: 
- description: The creators ratio metric measures the proportion of individuals who actively create content, such as reports, dashboards, or data visualizations, compared to those who primarily consume this content. A higher ratio indicates a robust self-service culture within the organization, suggesting that more users are empowered to generate insights independently rather than relying solely on centralized data teams. This metric reflects the level of engagement and proficiency among users in utilizing Business Intelligence tools. It also highlights the effectiveness of training and resources provided to foster a data-driven environment. Monitoring this ratio can help organizations identify areas for improvement in user adoption and content governance.

