- description: The Governance Coverage metric quantifies the extent to which governance signals, such as data certification, ownership assignments, and metadata documentation, are applied across business intelligence assets. A high coverage score indicates that a significant proportion of assets are well-managed, with clear ownership and defined quality standards, facilitating trust and reliability in decision-making processes. Conversely, low coverage suggests that many assets lack proper governance, which can lead to data inconsistencies, compliance risks, and challenges in data utilization. This metric serves as a critical indicator of the overall health of the BI governance framework, highlighting areas that require attention to ensure effective data stewardship. By monitoring governance coverage, organizations can better align their BI initiatives with strategic objectives and enhance the value derived from their data assets.

