Metric:
- id: decision.traceability
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the extent to which decisions made within the Business Intelligence (BI) framework are documented and connected to governed dashboards and data lineage. It assesses the clarity and accessibility of the relationships between decision points and the underlying data sources, ensuring that users can trace back the rationale behind each decision. Higher traceability indicates a robust governance structure, where evidence-based insights are readily available for review and validation. This transparency fosters trust in the BI system and enhances the overall decision-making process. The scope of this metric includes all logged decisions, their associated dashboards, and any cross-links to other relevant data elements.

