- description: This metric measures the occurrence of consecutive breaches of Service Level Agreements (SLAs) related to data refresh cycles within a Business Intelligence environment. It highlights patterns of systemic reliability risks by tracking the number of times the data refresh fails to meet the agreed-upon timelines. A streak of SLA breaches can indicate underlying issues in data processing, infrastructure, or resource allocation that may affect the overall quality and timeliness of decision support. By monitoring these streaks, organizations can proactively address reliability concerns and improve the consistency of data availability for end-users. This metric is crucial for maintaining trust in BI systems and ensuring that stakeholders have access to timely and accurate information for their decision-making processes.

